cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "RS Corridor Flood Watch: flood-potential thresholds (EDI, API) for the BR-116, BR-386 and BR-290 corridors, Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Andrade
    given-names: Valkiria
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/valkiriaandrade/rs-corridor-flood-watch"
abstract: >-
  Independent study that calibrates and validates, out of sample and against S2iD municipal flood records, flood-potential
  thresholds based on the Effective Drought Index (EDI) and the Antecedent Precipitation Index (API) computed on upstream-basin
  MERGE rainfall, and applies the frozen rules to ECMWF and GFS forecasts. Pre-registered protocol in docs/protocol.md;
  negative results are reported. Not an official warning.
keywords:
  - flood
  - effective drought index
  - antecedent precipitation index
  - forecast verification
  - Rio Grande do Sul
  - S2iD
